{
  "slug": "banner-of-kings",
  "family": "tracks",
  "label": "Banner of Kings",
  "note": "original — written in the idiom of the Game of Thrones main title (Ramin Djawadi, 2011), not transcribed from it. C natural minor, Aeolian throughout with no leading tone, driven at 128 BPM in 4/4 rather than the processional 6/8 (rowLen 2584, rows are 32nds so one pattern is one bar; 128 is not exactly representable — the row length lands on 2583.98 samples, so the grid runs at 127.999 BPM). 20 bars, loops at 37.50022675736962 s. 4 bars of ostinato alone, theme A Cm Cm Ab Ab / Eb Eb Bb Bb, theme B a fourth up Fm Fm Cm Cm / Ab Ab Bb Cm cadencing back to the bare ostinato. 7 ch: cello_ostinato = the engine (eight eighths a bar that never rest — root, fifth, third, fifth, root, fifth, third, fifth below — transposed onto each chord), low_drone = one sustained root a bar from bar 3, theme_strings = the melody (Eb4-C5 in theme A, restated an octave up in theme B and peaking on Bb5), dulcimer = the top of the ostinato struck an octave up, off the beat, entering at bar 9, base_tom = the war drum on a syncopated 1-and-of-2-and-of-3 pulse, bass_drum_4 = four on the floor, snare_2 = the backbeat with 16th fills closing bars 12 and 20.",
